  [scribe] skipped for hyp-20260906-003-r11s2: Command '['codex', '--ask-for-approval', 'never', 'exec', '-C', '.', '--sandbox', 'workspace-write', '--skip-git-repo-check', '--json', '--output-last-message', '/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/astra-max-20260905/bench-runs/gpt-6-astra_max-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/.scribe.hyp-20260906-003-r11s2.last', '--model', 'gpt-6-astra', '-c', 'model_reasoning_effort=max', 'You are a scribe distilling one-line research lessons.\n\nA CPU microarchitecture experiment just finished on cores/bench/. Your job\nis to append AT MOST ONE bullet to cores/bench/LESSONS.md summarizing what\nwas learned, OR write nothing at all if no useful lesson can be distilled.\n\n## This iteration\n\n- id:        hyp-20260906-003-r11s2\n- title:     Condition-aware bias for the existing agree predictor\n- category:  predictor\n- outcome:   regression\n- fitness:   360.92\n- delta_pct: -22.79%\n- error:     none\n\nMotivation:\nThe retained r4s2 winner uses 32 private two-bit counters to predict agreement\nwith the displacement sign. The predictor history in experiments/log.jsonl\nshows that additional capacity, global history, shared hysteresis, private\nGray recoding, loop tracking, and polarity banking all lost fitness. The\nr10s2 polarity-bank experiment reduced modeled errors but changed counter\nallocation and lookup structure, then lost 26.04% fitness. A smaller remaining\nopportunity is to improve the meaning of agreement while preserving the\nwinning table, PC hash, local update circuits, and training latency.\n\nReplaying the archived r9s2 branch-event trace gives 47235 direction errors\nfor the current bias and 43017 for the proposed bias over 529588 conditional\nbranches inside the timing markers: 4218 fewer errors, about 8.93%. Both\nmodels include all preceding warmup events and identical binary saturating\ncounters. The retained trace-source RTL matches the current bench RTL byte\nfor byte. This model updates in retirement order and omits fetch timing,\nqueued training, and candidate-dependent stalls; these are not measured\ncandidate cycles or Fmax. The trace is from the existing scored 2000-byte\nELF documented in prior implementation notes, distinct from the requested\nsupplemental 6000-byte validation. Neither workload nor evaluator may change.\n\n\nHypothesis:\nMake one predictor-policy change: define a conditional branch\'s static\nagreement bias as B = instruction[31] OR instruction[12]. Instruction bit\n12 is funct3[0]. Thus legal BNE, BGE, and BGEU start with a taken bias in\neither displacement direction; BEQ, BLT, and BLTU retain backward-taken,\nforward-not-taken bias. Every branch can still learn the opposite direction.\nThis fixed instruction-based rule applies to all programs and addresses;\nit uses no benchmark detection, PC-specific constants, or preloaded outcomes.\n\nIn IF, compute B from raw imem_data and use\nbranch_direction = B XOR !agree_msb. Keep legal-branch predecode, PC and\ntarget alignment eligibility, the shared B/J target adder, and accepted\npred_taken handling exactly as they are. The extra OR and existing bias\ninversion form a three-input Boolean function of instruction[31],\ninstruction[12], and agree_msb, which can fit in one LUT4; confirm actual\nmapping rather than assuming that this preserves whole-core Fmax.\n\nIn EX, use the identical bias expression from the resolving instruction:\nbranch_train_agree = (branch_cond == (in.instr[31] | in.instr[12])).\nKeep branch_train_valid\'s existing valid, legal, nontrapping, advancing-EX\nqualification, including reset, dmem-hold, and divider-wait exclusions.\nUse the fully forwarded actual branch condition, never pred_taken, to\ngenerate this event. IF prediction and EX training must use the same rule.\n\nPreserve branch_predictor.sv\'s binary counters and reset value 11, the\nPC[6:2] XOR PC[11:7] index, all 32 private entries, MSB-only lookup, and\nseven-bit registered training event. Pending events still drain exactly\nonce, reset cancels them, and lookup retains old-state semantics with no\ntraining bypass. No new predictor state, banks, tags, history, ports, or\npipeline metadata are needed. JAL prediction, JALR fallback, EX recovery,\narchitectural pc_next, traps, memory behavior, and nret=1 RVFI remain intact.\n\nValidate all six branch conditions, both displacement signs, and both actual\noutcomes against an independent bias-and-counter model. Explicitly exercise\nforward inverse-condition branches that agree and disagree with their new\ncold taken bias, delayed learning through both direction changes, aliases,\naccepted predictions across a counter update, reset, load-use forwarding,\ndmem holds, and divider holds. Preserve wrong-path-store suppression, exact\nretirement order and PC chaining, reserved-encoding and alignment traps,\nand existing saturation/event-queue assertions. Rework directed stimuli\nwhere their old bias assumptions no longer reach the intended state.\n\nRun the unchanged correctness and FPGA fitness gates and the requested\n6000-byte CRC/marker validation. Compare actual bracketed cycles and median\nFmax from all three prescribed routing seeds separately. The direction-model\nimprovement suggests only a small cycle opportunity; even a small Fmax loss\ncould erase it. The integer +1% fitness forecast is an optimistic, low-\nconfidence hypothesis, not a conversion of modeled errors into measured\nthroughput. No evaluation contract or other core is an editing target.\n\n\nExpected impact:\n{\'fitness_delta_pct\': 1, \'confidence\': \'low\'}\n\nImplementation notes (the implementing agent\'s self-report):\nImplemented the condition-aware agree bias. Correctness passes, but measured\nfitness regresses by 22.78790990%: 360.92117562 versus 467.44127138 iterations/s.\nThe 4,689-cycle scored improvement is outweighed by lower routed Fmax. The\nrequested implementation remains in place for the orchestrator to evaluate.\n\nChanged only two RTL expressions and their comments:\n\n- `cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv`: conditional direction is now\n  `(imem_data[31] | imem_data[12]) ^ !agree_msb`. The comment documents cold\n  taken prediction for BNE/BGE/BGEU in either displacement direction and\n  backward-taken/forward-not-taken prediction for BEQ/BLT/BLTU.\n- `cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv`: training agreement is now\n  `(branch_cond == (in.instr[31] | in.instr[12]))`, using the existing fully\n  forwarded actual condition. The advancing, valid, legal, nontrapping EX\n  qualification, including reset, dmem and divider exclusions, is unchanged.\n\nThere are no architectural deviations. The 32 private binary counters,\nreset-to-11 policy, PC[6:2] XOR PC[11:7] hash, MSB-only lookup, seven-bit\nregistered event, old-counter acceptance, and exactly-once event draining\nare unchanged. `branch_predictor.sv` and its standalone unit test are\nbyte-for-byte unchanged from HEAD. There are no new ports, state, tags,\nhistory, banks, metadata, prediction bypasses, or workload-specific rules.\nPredecode legality, PC/target alignment, shared B/J target addition,\naccepted prediction handling, JAL/JALR, EX recovery, architectural pc_next,\ntraps, memory behavior and the declared nret=1 RVFI interface are unchanged.\n\nUpdated `test_pipeline.py` and, beyond the advisory file list,\n`test_if_stage.py` to cover the changed IF policy directly. The independent\noracle derives bias semantically from the decoded condition and signed\nbranch displacement; it uses the existing independent arithmetic counter\nand queued-event model. It checks prediction before every edge, training\nqualification and agreement, pending events, all 32 counters, held payloads,\nand accepted directions against the previous cycle. Retirement-side events\nmust exactly match EX events, with full unchanged ISS/RVFI comparison,\ncontiguous order, PC chaining and accepted memory transaction checks.\n\nDirected coverage includes:\n\n- All six legal conditions